  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nAnomalously strong mid level ridge extending from the lower \nMississippi Valley into the Great Lakes will continue to offer \ndry weather and above normal temperatures. This ridge will \ngradually lose amplitude with the westerlies settling south \ninto the Ohio Valley thru mid week. The flow will briefly become \nzonal at mid week with low amplitude ridging returning late in the \nweek. \n\nA weak surface front will sag south into the area Monday into Monday\nnight and then wash out by Tuesday night into Wednesday. In the dry\nair mass only expect some increase in clouds from this front.  \nOtherwise, high pressure will predominate, so an extended dry period\nwill persist.\n\nTemperatures will remain above normal, with highs in the lower and\nmiddle 70s thru mid week warming into the mid and upper 70s by \nthe end of the week. Lows in the 40s to warm to the 50s by the end of\nthe week.",
